                                                "sense_id": "56182bbc-24c4-39b7-94d3-33d15b91a76f",
                                                "text": "1962 [Prentice-Hall], Kenneth Hoffman, Banach Spaces of Analytic Functions, 2007, Dover, page 138,\nBefore taking up the extreme points for H¹ and H ᪲, let us make a few elementary observations about the unit ball Σ in the Banach space X."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0aa1e434-bf67-4ec7-b544-6a593e2adfaf",
                                                "sense_id": "56182bbc-24c4-39b7-94d3-33d15b91a76f",
                                                "text": "Already in these cases there is convergence in Banach spaces that are not only infinite-dimensional but nonseparable."
